# OpenRouter

> One API for text, image, video, and audio models. Hundreds of models from
> many providers behind one API key, with routing, fallbacks, and cost tracking.

## What OpenRouter is and when to use it

OpenRouter is one OpenAI-compatible API in front of hundreds of text, image,
video, and audio models from many providers. Send
`POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions` with an OpenRouter API key
and a `model` such as `openai/gpt-4o` or `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4`.
Every chat model accepts that same request shape. Media models use one
dedicated endpoint per modality, with the same API key and the same bill:

- Image generation: `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images`. Guide: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-generation.md. Models: https://openrouter.ai/collections/image-models. Model API: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images/models.
- Video generation: `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/videos` (submit a job, poll it, download the clip). Guide: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/video-generation.md. Models: https://openrouter.ai/collections/video-models. Model API: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/videos/models.
- Text-to-speech: `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/audio/speech`. Guide: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/tts.md. Models: https://openrouter.ai/collections/text-to-speech-models. Model API: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/audio/speech/models.
- Speech-to-text: `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/audio/transcriptions`. Guide: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/stt.md. Models: https://openrouter.ai/collections/speech-to-text-models.
- Vision (image and PDF understanding): `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions` or `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses` with image or PDF inputs. Guides: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-understanding.md and https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/pdfs.md. Models: https://openrouter.ai/collections/vision-models.

Each model's per-model guide below gives the exact request for that model.

Use OpenRouter when you need to:

- Call many models or providers through one API key, one bill, and one SDK.
- Switch models without changing code, or compare models on the same prompt.
- Route around provider outages and rate limits with automatic fallbacks.
- Use text, image, video, speech-to-text, and text-to-speech models from one place.

OpenRouter is a managed LLM gateway, also called an AI gateway. OpenRouter hosts it, so there is nothing to deploy or self-host. See "LLM gateway comparisons" below for how it compares with self-hosted and other gateways.

Getting started:

- API keys are self-serve: sign up at https://openrouter.ai and create a key at https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys. No sales contact is needed.
- Free tier: models with the `:free` variant cost nothing, and the free models router at `openrouter/free` picks one for you. Free usage is rate limited per day; buying credits raises the limit. See https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/limits.md.
- Pricing is pay-as-you-go with no markup on the provider's price: per token for text models; per image, per second of video, or per character or minute of audio for media models: https://openrouter.ai/pricing.
- MCP server for agents: https://mcp.openrouter.ai/mcp (OAuth in the browser, hosted by OpenRouter). Setup guide: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/mcp-server.md.
- OpenAPI description of the whole API: https://openrouter.ai/openapi.json.

## Docs

- [Quickstart](https://openrouter.ai/docs/quickstart.md): Get an API key and send the first request.
- [API reference](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/overview.md): Endpoints, parameters, and response shapes.
- [Docs index](https://openrouter.ai/docs/llms.txt): Every documentation page as a markdown link with a one-line summary.
- [Full docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/llms-full.txt): The complete documentation in one file, for agents that want everything at once.
- [Limits](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/limits.md): Credit limits, free-model request caps, and rate limits.
- [Free variant](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/model-variants/free.md): Access free models with the `:free` variant.
- [Free models router](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/routers/free-router.md): Route to whichever free model is available.
- [FAQ](https://openrouter.ai/docs/faq.md): Common questions about billing, privacy, routing, and models.

## Models

- [Models](https://openrouter.ai/models): Compare every text, image, video, and audio model on OpenRouter by pricing, context length, and benchmarks, all through one API.
- [Model API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models): Machine-readable list of every model, with pricing and supported parameters.
- [Image models API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images/models): Machine-readable list of image generation models; fetch `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images/models/{author}/{slug}/endpoints` for per-endpoint parameters and pricing.
- [Video models API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/videos/models): Machine-readable list of video generation models with supported aspect ratios, durations, resolutions, and pricing.
- [Speech models API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/audio/speech/models): Machine-readable list of text-to-speech models; fetch `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/audio/speech/models/{author}/{slug}` for per-model voices and speech parameters.
- Per-model guide: `https://openrouter.ai/{author}/{model}/llms.txt` returns one machine-readable guide with sections for every confirmed OpenRouter API that serves a public model: text/chat, image, video, speech-to-text, and text-to-speech.

## Site

- [Rankings](https://openrouter.ai/rankings): LLM leaderboards by real-world usage, ranked by tokens processed through the OpenRouter API, with per-modality views.
- [Pricing](https://openrouter.ai/pricing.md): How OpenRouter pricing works, with pay-as-you-go and enterprise plans, plus answers to common billing questions. Markdown twin of https://openrouter.ai/pricing with the plan table, fees, BYOK terms, and billing FAQ.
- [Enterprise](https://openrouter.ai/enterprise.md): OpenRouter for companies: one API, contract, and invoice for every model, with SSO and SCIM, zero data retention and in-region routing, budgets and spend alerts, invoiced billing, and an SLA. Talk to sales at https://openrouter.ai/enterprise/form. Markdown twin of https://openrouter.ai/enterprise with the security controls, billing terms, and FAQ.
- [Providers](https://openrouter.ai/providers): The network of model providers available on OpenRouter, with a page per provider.
- [Compare](https://openrouter.ai/compare): Compare models by benchmarks, price, context length, latency, uptime, and throughput.
- [Collections](https://openrouter.ai/collections.md): Curated collections of models, including free models and image generation models. Markdown twin of https://openrouter.ai/collections; per-collection guide at `https://openrouter.ai/collections/{slug}/llms.txt`.
- [Image generation models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/image-models): Image generation models ranked by weekly usage; generate images from text prompts and reference images with one API.
- [Video generation models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/video-models): Video generation models ranked by weekly usage; generate videos from text or images with one API and compare per-second pricing.
- [Text-to-speech models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/text-to-speech-models): Text-to-speech models for voice generation, narration, assistants, accessibility, and audio apps.
- [Speech-to-text models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/speech-to-text-models): Speech-to-text and transcription models for meetings, calls, captions, and speech recognition.
- [Audio generation models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/audio-models): Audio generation models for music, sound, and audio-output applications.
- [Vision models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/vision-models): Multimodal vision models ranked by weekly usage for image analysis, OCR, document/PDF extraction, and visual reasoning.
- [Apps](https://openrouter.ai/apps): App and agent rankings, listing the apps built on OpenRouter and the top apps by category.
- [State of AI](https://openrouter.ai/state-of-ai): An empirical study of real-world LLM usage across more than 100 trillion tokens on OpenRouter.
- [Data](https://openrouter.ai/data): OpenRouter's empirical AI usage data for researchers, journalists, and academics.
- [Support](https://openrouter.ai/support): Frequently asked questions about using OpenRouter, and how to reach support.
- [For AI crawlers](https://openrouter.ai/for-ai): Text-only HTML index of the site with the top models per modality, every provider, and every collection, each with a description and canonical link.

## LLM gateway comparisons

- [LLM gateway guide](https://openrouter.ai/blog/insights/llm-gateway/): What an LLM gateway does, with a table comparing OpenRouter, LiteLLM, Portkey, Helicone, Kong AI Gateway, TrueFoundry AI Gateway, Bifrost, and llmgateway.io on self-hosting, model coverage, pricing, failover, observability, and compliance.
- [OpenRouter vs LiteLLM](https://openrouter.ai/blog/insights/openrouter-vs-litellm/): Managed gateway versus self-hosted proxy, compared on cost, data residency, RBAC, routing, and setup time.
- [OpenRouter vs Portkey](https://openrouter.ai/blog/insights/openrouter-vs-portkey/): Managed routing network versus AI control plane, compared on models, governance, compliance, and price.

## EU in-region routing

- [OpenRouter EU](https://openrouter.ai/business/eu): EU in-region routing on OpenRouter Business. Requests sent to https://eu.openrouter.ai are decrypted in the EU and routed only to shared provider endpoints located in Europe (the EU/EEA, the UK, and Switzerland); prompts and completions are processed there, while account data, billing records, authentication data, security logs, and other operational records may be stored and processed in the US. Requests served by a customer's BYOK key go to the customer's own cloud deployment: the customer provisions it in the region they need and sets the key's region per provider, and OpenRouter does not verify where it runs. Self-serve on Business: no contract, no monthly minimum. Lists the live EU model catalog, the data boundary, and data-region guardrail setup.
- [EU Model API](https://eu.openrouter.ai/api/v1/models): Machine-readable list of models with endpoints in Europe (the EU/EEA, the UK, and Switzerland), with EU endpoint pricing. Batch (:batch) variants appear in this list but are not accepted on regional domains; the Batch API runs only on openrouter.ai.
- [In-region routing docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/features/in-region-routing): Regional base URLs, fail-closed behavior, and the features regional domains reject.

## Ori

- [Ori](https://openrouter.ai/ori): OpenRouter's family of tools for putting agents to work with any model: Ori Harness, Ori Code, Ori Eval, Ori Intern, and Ori Desktop.
- [Ori Harness](https://openrouter.ai/ori/harness): Run the agent CLI you already use — Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Hermes, and more — on OpenRouter, with OAuth sign-in and your org's guardrails.
- [Ori Eval](https://openrouter.ai/ori/eval.md): Find the best model for your project — run your agent on your own prompts, on a harness and model that stay pinned, and rank the candidates.
- [spawn-ori-eval skill](https://openrouter.ai/skills/spawn-ori-eval): For coding agents. Read it to run a model eval by handing it to Ori, so the eval is authored and graded on a pinned harness and model rather than one you improvised.
- [install-ori-harness skill](https://openrouter.ai/skills/install-ori-harness): For coding agents. Read it to install Ori, sign in, run an existing agent CLI through Ori, choose an OpenRouter model, and verify the setup.
- [Install Ori](https://openrouter.ai/labs/ori/install.sh): `curl -fsSL https://openrouter.ai/labs/ori/install.sh | bash`
- [Ori Harness docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/ori/harness.md): Installing Ori, signing in, and running each supported agent CLI on OpenRouter.

## Skills

- [Skills](https://github.com/OpenRouterTeam/skills): Every skill OpenRouter publishes. Each one is served as raw markdown from `https://openrouter.ai/skills/<name>` (also at `/.well-known/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, for agents that look there first).
- [Agent guide](https://openrouter.ai/agents.md): Using OpenRouter from a coding agent.

## Benchmarks

- [Benchmarks](https://openrouter.ai/benchmarks): Browse live independent benchmark results for OpenRouter models, providers, and search engines.
- [Image benchmarks](https://openrouter.ai/benchmarks/media/images): Side-by-side image model outputs across curated prompts.
- [Video benchmarks](https://openrouter.ai/benchmarks/media/videos): Side-by-side video model outputs across curated prompts.
- [Speech benchmarks](https://openrouter.ai/benchmarks/media/speech): Side-by-side text-to-speech model audio takes across curated prompts.
- [GET /api/v1/benchmarks](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/benchmarks): Fetch benchmark results programmatically with a valid OpenRouter API key.
- [Benchmarks API reference](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/benchmarks/list-benchmarks): Read the API contract for listing benchmark results and supported filters.
